            <ArticleTitle>Endocrine aspects of headaches in children and adolescents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>331-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Headaches due to endocrine diseases in childhood are rare, but any child with chronic headaches should be given serious consideration. The most serious etiology is a tumor of the hypothalamic-pituitary region. Headaches can also occur as premenstrual migraine or as water retention due to glucocorticoid or Growth Hormone (GH) overdosage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
